     "answer": 0,
     "explain": "By March 1933, bank runs had closed thousands of banks. Roosevelt declared a national bank holiday, Congress passed the Emergency Banking Act within days, and his first Fireside Chat helped restore confidence. The FDIC was created later in 1933.",
